{
  "requirement": "The SDK formats node inputs using `Contents::format_node_content`,\ndefined by {cite}`requirements.sdk.graph.fingerprinting.fingerprint_content`:\n\n```rust,ignore\n// Method on Contents. Both arguments describe the already-read snapshot.\n/// Present these supplied contents as text for an agent.\nfn format_node_content(\n    &self,\n    node: &Self::NodeId,\n    contents: &Self::NodeContent,\n) -> Result<String, Self::Error>;\n```\n\nThe formatter uses the supplied contents; their fingerprint describes the same\nread. For inputs queued on an ask builder, formatting errors return\n`ValidationError::Graph`. During a `read_node` tool call, a formatting error is\nreturned to the agent as a tool error, so it can continue and recover.\n`NodeContent` and `NodeId` retain their application-defined types without\nserialization or display bounds.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The reviewed tests cover each obligation in `requirements.sdk.graph.agent-calls.judge.rendering`.\n\n- **Formatting through `Contents::format_node_content` for queued inputs.**\n  - `explicit_insertions_preserve_order_repetition_and_selection_snapshots` queues current-node and successor contents. It asserts that the agent receives the formatted text in order.\n  - It also asserts the node reads are exactly `[1, 3, 2, 3, 1]`. The formatter therefore works on the supplied snapshot, and nothing is reread.\n  - `default_tool_accepts_scalar_results_and_keeps_the_exact_prefix` checks that the delivered user message contains the formatted content.\n  - `behavioral_adequacy_uses_domain_contents_and_returns_a_typed_fingerprinted_answer` checks that the formatted text of both nodes reaches the agent in order. It also checks that each node was read once.\n- **Formatter uses the supplied contents, and the fingerprint describes the same read.**\n  - `identities_remain_stable_and_fingerprinting_uses_the_supplied_snapshot` formats the snapshot, then changes the underlying content. It asserts that formatting still yields \"before\", matching the snapshot's fingerprint, and that only one read happened.\n  - `domain_formats_supplied_contents_without_resolving_a_replacement` shows the real `HabeasDomain` formatter using supplied contents for a file that does not exist on disk. It also checks that a mismatched node type returns an error.\n  - `authoring_keeps_the_prepared_subject_snapshot_and_concrete_version` and `runner_does_not_store_a_missing_agent_error_and_supports_intermediate_calls` check that the recorded dependency fingerprints match the supplied reads.\n- **Formatting errors for queued inputs return `ValidationError::Graph`.**\n  - `queued_reads_selection_and_rendering_fail_before_agent_invocation` sets `fail_format`. It asserts `Err(ValidationError::Graph(\"render\"))`, no recorded dependencies, and no agent call.\n- **Formatting errors during a `read_node` tool call are returned to the agent as a tool error.**\n  - `node_rendering_tool_errors_allow_recovery_without_recording_undelivered_contents` makes the formatter fail. The agent receives a tool result with `is_error`, the name `read_node` and the error text. The agent then submits successfully. The test also asserts that no dependency was recorded for contents that were never delivered.\n- **Successful `read_node` rendering.** `validator_agent_executions_isolate_conversations_and_dependency_traces` and the concurrent-agent tests use the `distinct_pages` formatter, which covers the successful path.\n- **No serialization or display bounds on `NodeContent` and `NodeId`.** This is a compile-time constraint. The test fixtures use plain application types such as `Node(u8)` and `Content(String)` with the formatter, and they compile.\n\nI found no unexercised obligation or weak assertion.",
  "references": "be8dfa22dce3f9297803609deae03b7b9d0aafd2150eb790d6da62f8e199b8aa",
